you're talking about.

00:00:21.254 --> 00:00:22.222 line:92%
-I got five innocent victims

00:00:22.222 --> 00:00:24.724 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you're asking me to stan
down on the ring leader?

00:00:24.724 --> 00:00:27.160 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's not an ask.
It's a direct order.

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:29.696 align:start size:94% position:6%
Sometimes we have to
make compromises

00:00:29.696 --> 00:00:30.764 size:78% position:39% line:92%
for the greater good.

00:00:30.764 --> 00:00:31.798 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Bull[bleep]

00:00:31.798 --> 00:00:33.266 line:92%
This man lost his only child

00:00:33.266 --> 00:00:39.305 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you of all people should b
able to relate to that.

00:00:39.305 --> 00:00:40.940 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Mother[bleep], get out.

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:44.277 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Welcome to the show
Titus Welliver.

00:00:44.277 --> 00:00:45.712 line:92%
Nice to see you, my friend

00:00:45.712 --> 00:00:48.114 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That was an introduction.
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:48.114 --> 00:00:52.218
We like to introduce peopl
by another actor telling the

00:00:52.218 --> 00:00:53.753 size:84% position:42% line:92%
to get the [bleep] out.

00:00:53.753 --> 00:00:54.521 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.521 --> 00:00:57.991
-I couldn't tell you how man
times Reddick and I did that

00:00:57.991 --> 00:01:00.493 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I couldn't keep
a straight face.

00:01:00.493 --> 00:01:03.930 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's acting right there.
I'll tell you.

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:05.098 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-Yeah. Lance Reddick.

00:01:05.098 --> 00:01:08.802 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, one of the great joy
of the show "Bosch"

00:01:08.802 --> 00:01:11.905 align:start size:94% position:6%
is how frustrated
he is with you constantly.

00:01:11.905 --> 00:01:13.073 size:81% position:41% line:92%
Through seven seasons,

00:01:13.073 --> 00:01:15.842 align:start size:94% position:6%
he's never gotten used to
Bosch's behavior.

00:01:15.842 --> 00:01:16.876 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-No, no, not at all.

00:01:16.876 --> 00:01:19.712 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, you know, the thing about
it is that people say,

00:01:19.712 --> 00:01:21.881 size:78% position:39%
"Oh, Lance Reddick --
he's really intense."

00:01:21.881 --> 00:01:25.785 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I go, "He's a complete
Boo Boo the Fool."

00:01:25.785 --> 00:01:26.653 size:78% position:39% line:92%
We joke all the time.

00:01:26.653 --> 00:01:27.620 align:start size:94% position:6%
We call each other
Boo Boo the fool

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:33.326 align:start size:94% position:6%
because all we do is talk abou
comic books, "Star Trek."

00:01:33.326 --> 00:01:35.361 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
He's silly.

00:01:35.361 --> 00:01:36.162 size:88% position:44% line:92%
He's a silly, silly guy.

00:01:36.162 --> 00:01:40.467
But, you know, when they cal
"action," he goes into lockdown.

00:01:40.467 --> 00:01:44.871 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, certainly in the roles
I know him for,

00:01:44.871 --> 00:01:46.206 size:81% position:41% line:92%
very little silliness.

00:01:46.206 --> 00:01:50.510
I first became familiar with you
on "Lost," and I think

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:52.512 align:start size:94% position:6%
because of that,
it never occurred to me

00:01:52.512 --> 00:01:54.647 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you were
a fellow New Englander.

00:01:54.647 --> 00:01:56.883 align:start size:94% position:6%
You grew up in Maine.
Is that right?

00:01:56.883 --> 00:02:00.787
-I spent my summers there, and I
went to boarding school there.

00:02:00.787 --> 00:02:06.392
So I had -- I spent a lot of
time in Maine and in Boston,

00:02:06.392 --> 00:02:11.464
and in -- you know, your neck of
the woods, not Franconia,

00:02:11.464 --> 00:02:15.135 size:88% position:44% line:92%
but a lot of time there.

00:02:15.135 --> 00:02:18.004 size:78% position:39%
So I consider myself
a New Englander 100%.

00:02:18.004 --> 00:02:20.707 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I think the highest
praise you can get as an actor

00:02:20.707 --> 00:02:25.645
from New England is being cast
in multiple Ben Affleck movies

00:02:25.645 --> 00:02:26.346 size:88% position:44% line:92%
which has been the case.

00:02:26.346 --> 00:02:30.583 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, that's not a guy
who doesn't have an ear for it

00:02:30.583 --> 00:02:33.186 line:92%
-That's true. That's true.

00:02:33.186 --> 00:02:36.022 align:start size:94% position:6%
When I went in and met him
for "Gone Baby Gone,"

00:02:36.022 --> 00:02:38.525 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I was doing
the audition thing,

00:02:38.525 --> 00:02:39.792 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I said,
"Here, you know what?

00:02:39.792 --> 00:02:42.095 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'll do it again,
and I'll dial the accent down.

00:02:42.095 --> 00:02:45.398
And he went, "No, no, no, no
no, no, please, keep it there.

00:02:45.398 --> 00:02:49.235
And then we would get on set
and I would do, you know, a take

00:02:49.235 --> 00:02:52.205
and he'd come over and he woul
say, "I'm losing the accent.

00:02:52.205 --> 00:02:55.675 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I would say,
"Ben, if I go any harder,

00:02:55.675 --> 00:02:56.809 line:92%
we're going to need subtitles.

00:02:56.809 --> 00:02:59.779
And he said, "I don't care
It's got to be grounded."

00:02:59.779 --> 00:03:03.516
And I was relieved because
with the exception I think o

00:03:03.516 --> 00:03:07.954 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Good Will Hunting"
and prior to that was

00:03:07.954 --> 00:03:08.788 line:92%
"The Friends of Eddie Coyle,

00:03:08.788 --> 00:03:13.660 align:start size:94% position:6%
which was, like,
the quintessential Boston film

00:03:13.660 --> 00:03:14.827 line:92%
because everything else wa

00:03:14.827 --> 00:03:17.630 size:81% position:41%
a bad "Pepperidge Farm
Remembers" commercial,

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:19.966 align:start size:94% position:6%
which was so offensive,
I'm sure to you.

00:03:19.966 --> 00:03:24.804 size:84% position:42%
When I hear that, I go,
"Better to not do it."

00:03:24.804 --> 00:03:30.376
-You also went to NYU with
a fellow from my hometown.

00:03:30.376 --> 00:03:33.513
He was there first, I should
establish, but Adam Sandler.

00:03:33.513 --> 00:03:36.282 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you guys were in a comed
writing class together.

00:03:36.282 --> 00:03:40.486
Did you have an early sens
of his talent in that field?

00:03:40.486 --> 00:03:43.656 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know, he's just one o
those guys that's always funny

00:03:43.656 --> 00:03:46.893 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so we ended up
in this class together,

00:03:46.893 --> 00:03:50.230 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I took it
just because it seemed lik

00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:53.333 align:start size:94% position:6%
an interesting class,
and I knew Adam.

00:03:53.333 --> 00:03:58.671
But we were immediately, after
the first class, were separate

00:03:58.671 --> 00:04:00.873 align:start size:94% position:6%
and were not allowed
to sit together anymore.

00:04:00.873 --> 00:04:02.242 line:92%
I mean, you know, we're at NYU

00:04:02.242 --> 00:04:04.544 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's not like we were
in third grade.

00:04:04.544 --> 00:04:05.278 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:05.278 --> 00:04:07.880 align:start size:94% position:6%
I would just look at him,
and he would say things like

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:11.317 size:81% position:41%
"I really can't wait
to get a cup of coffee

00:04:11.317 --> 00:04:13.753 align:start size:94% position:6%
and a bag of Cheetos."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:13.753 --> 00:04:17.023 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I would lose it
in the middle of the class

00:04:17.023 --> 00:04:21.995
You know, they would go, "Adam
Titus, guys, come on, please."

00:04:21.995 --> 00:04:27.500
And so it became, you know, we
thoroughly enjoyed torturing

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:30.003 line:92%
this poor assistant professor.

00:04:30.003 --> 00:04:33.072 size:84% position:42%
She deeply disliked us,
and I don't know why

00:04:33.072 --> 00:04:36.209
other than maybe she just ha
a thing about New Englanders

00:04:36.209 --> 00:04:39.112 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I was really kind of lucky
in that way,

00:04:39.112 --> 00:04:44.150
is that I got to see Adam, you
know, so early in his career

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:49.355
I would go and see him in little
comedy clubs all over Manhattan.

00:04:49.355 --> 00:04:51.658 line:92%
And, you know, he's an original.

00:04:51.658 --> 00:04:55.228 align:start size:94% position:6%
The stuff he was doing then wa
not -- You didn't say,

00:04:55.228 --> 00:04:56.596 line:92%
"Well, that reminds me of X.

00:04:56.596 --> 00:04:59.532 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was -- You know,
Sandler is his own guy.

00:04:59.532 --> 00:05:04.070 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you know, his success
has been, you know,

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:06.339 line:92%
a really nice thing to observe

00:05:06.339 --> 00:05:08.775 align:start size:94% position:6%
because he's a really good
human being.

00:05:08.775 --> 00:05:09.842 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He's one of
the all-time greats.

00:05:09.842 --> 00:05:14.380
I said to him that I don't think
he has a New Hampshire accen

00:05:14.380 --> 00:05:16.749 align:start size:94% position:6%
as much as every kid I grew up
with in New Hampshire

00:05:16.749 --> 00:05:19.719 align:start size:94% position:6%
had an Adam Sandler accent
because once he became famous,

00:05:19.719 --> 00:05:21.854
like, every kid I went to
high school with was like,

00:05:21.854 --> 00:05:22.689 line:92%
[as Sandler] "Oh, here we go."

00:05:22.689 --> 00:05:26.159
[ Normal voice ] I was like,
that's not a regional dialect.

00:05:26.159 --> 00:05:27.827 line:92%
You're just doing Adam Sandler

00:05:27.827 --> 00:05:31.597 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Nobody in New Hampshire
is talking like this.

00:05:31.597 --> 00:05:32.665 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:32.665 --> 00:05:35.802 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the ice cream --
"Eat your goddamn ice cream.

00:05:35.802 --> 00:05:37.537 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'll kill ya."
[ Laughter ]

00:05:37.537 --> 00:05:41.674
-I am always fascinated by early
roles that actors have.

00:05:41.674 --> 00:05:44.410 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you were sort of known for
playing, you know,

00:05:44.410 --> 00:05:49.482 align:start size:94% position:6%
in sort of grittier fare,
but you had a part in "90210."

00:05:49.482 --> 00:05:50.149 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
What was your part,

00:05:50.149 --> 00:05:52.952
and what was your father's
reaction when he saw it?

00:05:52.952 --> 00:05:58.791
-I played this guy who was thi
alcoholic boyfriend to this girl

00:05:58.791 --> 00:06:01.494 align:start size:94% position:6%
who was trying to make
a sober go of it.

00:06:01.494 --> 00:06:05.231 align:start size:94% position:6%
And Luke Perry --
God rest his soul --

00:06:05.231 --> 00:06:06.799 line:92%
was her sponsor and friend

00:06:06.799 --> 00:06:10.670
And my character was kind of
jealous and we got into a thing,

00:06:10.670 --> 00:06:15.908
and Luke Perry, who was
considerably smaller than I was,

00:06:15.908 --> 00:06:18.111 line:92%
took me out with one punch

00:06:18.111 --> 00:06:20.913
You know, he was laughing.
I mean, we had a great time.

00:06:20.913 --> 00:06:23.683 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he was a warm and welcomin
and lovely guy.

00:06:23.683 --> 00:06:27.887
But I didn't even tell my father
that I was on this thing.

00:06:27.887 --> 00:06:30.289
And I got a call from him
the next day, and he --

00:06:30.289 --> 00:06:33.459
calling from his house in Maine,
and he said, "Yeah, that thing

00:06:33.459 --> 00:06:36.729 align:start size:94% position:6%
you were on last night,
what is it?

00:06:36.729 --> 00:06:39.932 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Los Angeles 9-51-62."

00:06:39.932 --> 00:06:41.567 line:92%
I said, "Oh, yeah, '90210.'"

00:06:41.567 --> 00:06:43.770 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he went, "Yeah, well,
whatever it's called.

00:06:43.770 --> 00:06:44.971 line:92%
Don't ever do that again."

00:06:44.971 --> 00:06:47.473 size:88% position:44% line:92%
And I said, "What? Why?"

00:06:47.473 --> 00:06:50.309 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he went,
"Yeah, it's bad for your soul.

00:06:50.309 --> 00:06:50.843 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:06:50.843 --> 00:06:52.545 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I went, "Well, Dad,
I've got to pay my bills."

00:06:52.545 --> 00:06:55.415 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he said, "Son,
if you need money that badly

00:06:55.415 --> 00:06:57.650 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'll send you some."
[ Laughter ]

00:06:57.650 --> 00:06:58.818 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, that's
the kind of support

00:06:58.818 --> 00:07:01.087 align:start size:94% position:6%
every actor should be
lucky to have.

00:07:01.087 --> 00:07:03.689 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's a very kind thing
for a father to do for his son

00:07:03.689 --> 00:07:06.459 size:88% position:44%
-Yeah, the subtext was,
"Hold out for Scorsese."

00:07:06.459 --> 00:07:07.593 line:92%
And I was like, "Oh, okay.

00:07:07.593 --> 00:07:09.429 align:start size:94% position:6%
Right now I'm
in Jason Priestley Land,

00:07:09.429 --> 00:07:10.930 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I hope to get there
someday."

00:07:10.930 --> 00:07:13.533 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hey, congratulations so muc
on seven seasons.

00:07:13.533 --> 00:07:15.768 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thanks so much for making time
with us today.

00:07:15.768 --> 00:07:16.569 line:92%
It was great talking to you.

00:07:16.569 --> 00:07:18.271 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you.
Great talking to you.

00:07:18.271 --> 00:07:18.905 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It was a pleasure.

00:07:18.905 --> 00:07:20.606 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The seventh and final seaso
of "Bosch"

00:07:20.606 --> 00:07:23.976 align:start size:94% position:6%
premieres June 25th
on Amazon Prime Video.

